# Retired image paths.
#
# Image filenames carry a version so that changed bytes never reuse a URL (see
# _headers). The cost of that policy is that every previous filename 404s the
# moment it is renamed, which breaks any external link, embed, or social card
# that was scraped while the old name was live.
#
# These keep those references resolving to the current art instead of dying.
# One redirect per retired name, newest target on the right.
#
# These 301s also receive the /assets/* immutable Cache-Control from _headers,
# so a browser may keep following one for a year: never delete or reuse a
# target file; retire it with a redirect of its own instead.
/assets/hwinfo-sensors.webp        /assets/hwinfo-sensors-v4.webp        301
/assets/hwinfo-sensors-v2.webp     /assets/hwinfo-sensors-v4.webp        301
/assets/hwinfo-sensors-v3.webp     /assets/hwinfo-sensors-v4.webp        301
/assets/hwinfo-layouts.webp        /assets/hwinfo-layouts-v2.webp        301
/assets/streamdeck-plusxl.webp     /assets/streamdeck-plusxl-v2.webp     301
/assets/og-card-v1.jpg             /assets/og-card-v2.jpg                301
